{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py","line":116,"code_snippet":"group = entry.get(\"dispatch_group\") or block.get(\"dispatch_group\") or \"\"","reasoning_trace":"Compared the three readers of dispatch_group under hounfour.locality: local_voices. hop-locality.py:116 and config.ts:730 accept a provider-level key; cheval.py:541, openai_adapter.py:221 and modelinv.py:476 read the model entry only. A provider-level-only declaration is planned local, dispatched with no TransportPolicy, and recorded hop_locality: hosted. Dissent DISS-C-001 reached the same conclusion independently.","finding":"Three implementations of 'is this hop local' disagree on a provider-level dispatch_group","critique":"The posture's only control is a label read differently by the planner, Bridgebuilder and cheval; the audit chain contradicts the plan.","remediation":"Pick one reading. Either drop block.get(...) in hop-locality.py and the provider-level/every-model branches in isLocalVoice, or make _build_provider_config and hop_locality_of fall back to the provider block. Add a provider-level-only case to each test suite.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-668 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/668.html","CWE-778 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"availability","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":4335,"code_snippet":"if [[ $estimated_cost_cents -gt $budget ]]; then","reasoning_trace":"_adv_budget_estimate (line 3866) sums primary + companion first hop + advisory voices at catalog prices; the sum is compared to budget_cents, which .loa.config.yaml.example:1624 and :1690 still define as a cap on ONE dissent call. Reproduced with a dry run on pr/head.diff under this workspace's configured 200c: estimate 955c (primary gpt-5.5-pro 718c, companion claude-headless 237c), exit 4 budget_exceeded, before any dispatch. The audit's own dissent had to be run with --budget 1200.","finding":"Budget gate compares the sum over every planned voice against a documented per-call budget; the mandatory dissent refuses under shipped defaults","critique":"A contract change shipped without its default, comment or migration note. The security gate the framework makes mandatory stops running for ordinary diffs.","remediation":"Either compare per voice (max single-voice estimate) against budget_cents, or make it a run total and raise the example defaults, rewrite the two comments and add a migration line. Name the semantics in the envelope (per_voice|total).","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html","OWASP A05:2021 https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration/"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py","line":156,"code_snippet":"check_endpoint(endpoint, optin, name)","reasoning_trace":"validate_providers admits allow_insecure_endpoint for every non-CLI provider type. TransportPolicy is constructed only in openai_adapter.py (_transport_policy line 217, health_check line 858); anthropic_adapter.py:334 and google_adapter.py call http_post_stream/http_post with no policy. Executed: a type: anthropic provider with endpoint http://10.0.0.5:8080 and allow_insecure_endpoint 10.0.0.5 loads cleanly through the head loader. Dissent DISS-C-002 confirmed.","finding":"Insecure-endpoint opt-in is admitted for provider types whose adapter applies none of the promised request-time rules","critique":"The example config promises no proxy, no redirects and a path-prefix rule 'for this provider'; that holds for OpenAI-type providers only.","remediation":"Refuse allow_insecure_endpoint at load unless the provider type is openai/openai_compat, or construct the TransportPolicy in ProviderAdapter so every adapter's http_* call receives it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-319 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html","CWE-601 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/601.html","OWASP A10:2021 https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29/"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py","line":143,"code_snippet":"def validate_providers(merged: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:","reasoning_trace":"Nothing ties dispatch_group: local to a loopback/RFC1918/opt-in endpoint. Executed: hop-locality.py classifies lanbox:m1 (endpoint https://llm.example.com/v1, model dispatch_group: local) as local, and the head loader loads it. Under local_voices such a hop is planned, dispatched (TransportPolicy restricts proxies/redirects/path, not the destination) and recorded hop_locality: local.","finding":"The local_voices posture trusts the dispatch_group label; a hosted https endpoint labelled local is planned, dispatched and audited as local","critique":"The one control meant to keep prompts on the host is a self-declared label with no consistency check against the endpoint it governs.","remediation":"At load, warn or refuse when a dispatch_group: local model's provider endpoint is not loopback, RFC1918 or the provider's opt-in host; record the endpoint class beside hop_locality in MODELINV.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-807 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","CWE-778 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/openai_adapter.py","line":111,"code_snippet":"return \"response_format\" in text or \"json_schema\" in text","reasoning_trace":"Any HTTP 400 whose body mentions response_format or json_schema triggers one retry without the schema (lines 191-204). OpenAI strict-mode schema errors ('Invalid schema for response_format ...') match too, and a server controls both status and body. _build_chat_body always sends strict: true (line 441). The downgrade is recorded (schema_rejected_by_server) but not surfaced beyond a WARN. Review MEDIUM and dissent DISS-C-004 agree.","finding":"400 heuristic lets a supported-but-strict-rejecting server, or any hostile server, silently downgrade structured output and receive the prompt twice","critique":"The heuristic cannot distinguish 'unsupported feature' from 'your schema is wrong'; the operator who declared structured_json loses enforcement without a visible failure.","remediation":"Narrow to the error object's param/code fields; treat 'invalid schema'/'additionalProperties' phrasings as a schema defect (raise or retry once with strict: false); add the OpenAI strict-mode message as a negative case in test_the_heuristic.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-757 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/757.html","CWE-754 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/SKILL.md","line":118,"code_snippet":"exit keys follow the trusted-source precedence below even when the checkout is a PR head.","reasoning_trace":"loadTrustedConfig refuses only head-only keyless/insecure declarations (config.ts:684-686). Every voice dispatches through cheval, whose loader reads the working tree's .loa.config.yaml (the PR head on a PR-head checkout); validate_declared_endpoint admits any https DNS host. On such a checkout the head still controls the endpoint of a built-in provider and cheval would send that provider's credential to it. Pre-existing exposure (#1050 says no PR-head checkout is shipped), but the PR's new sentence claims protection in exactly that scenario.","finding":"Documented trusted-config protection is broader than the control: only two flags are refused, cheval's own config read is unprotected on a PR-head checkout","critique":"False assurance in the trust contract is itself a defect: an operator reading SKILL.md:118 could adopt a PR-head checkout believing provider declarations are trusted-source only.","remediation":"Either scope the sentence to what is refused (keyless and allow_insecure_endpoint), or pass the trusted provider view to cheval (e.g. a LOA_HOUNFOUR_TRUSTED_CONFIG path) so endpoints and aliases also come from the trusted source.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html","CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html"]}
